<p dir="auto">MTP acceptance stays flat at ~74.8% from 50k to 150k, so the remaining depth sag is attention cost, not speculative-decode decay. Before this PR the same card was ~8 t/s at 35k.</p>
<p dir="auto">So on G31 this is a clear win, both with and without MTP. But WizardlyBump17's B580 results going the other way are worth taking seriously before this merges. The gate here is <code class="notranslate">bmg_g21 || bmg_g31</code>, and if the win doesn't hold on G21, it'd be cleaner to gate TILE to G31 for now and let a B580 repro decide whether G21 gets it later, rather than ship a regression on one of the two dies it touches.</p>
<p dir="auto">If it helps narrow it: my B70 is a single card, q8_0 KV, and the +47% is no-MTP decode at 32k. Happy to run a specific config if someone wants to cross-check the G21/G31 difference on the same flags.</p>

